    "structuralMitigation": "The lowering makes strictness structural instead: every emitted pattern is exercised by `patterns_compile` inside the COMPLETE `result` rule, so a compile failure leaves `result` undefined and the entrypoint returns an EMPTY RESULT SET. Proven on a control (see `guardedControlResult`). The host contract then requires reading an empty result set as an ERROR ROW, never as a zero-violation verdict.",
